ey're going to  lose those rights unless they take  an action and a step and what that step  is  this is terrifying alex what happens  next well  campaigners have been pleading for  months for governments to be more  lenient  and the netherlands has already agreed  to make sure that they keep their  residency scheme open until the end of  the year  partly because of covid 19. the british  government has just said  that they will start issuing 28-day  notices  to people to warn them that they've got  to apply so they means people have got a  few more weeks but that's not much  and then other countries such as france  well we haven't heard any anything more  so it does mean that there are tens of  thousands if not hundreds of thousands  of people  who could suddenly find that their lives  have been turned upside down  but you're in good shape we're not going  to lose you hopefully i'm in good shape  our fingers are crossed alex forest  whining as always alex thank you  you


